.TH "RTCRTPSENDER.DTMF" "3JS" "September 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCRtpSender.dtmf \- RTCRtpSender: dtmf property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The read\-only \f[B]\f[CB]dtmf\f[B]\f[R] property on the
\f[CR]RTCRtpSender\f[R] interface returns an \f[CR]RTCDTMFSender\f[R]
you can use to send DTMF tones on this sender\(cqs audio track.
.SH VALUE
An \f[CR]RTCDTMFSender\f[R] if this is an audio sender, or
\f[CR]null\f[R] if it isn\(cqt.
.PP
Each audio sender gets its own \f[CR]RTCDTMFSender\f[R] when it\(cqs
created, so a connection sending two audio tracks has two of them.
Senders for video tracks return \f[CR]null\f[R].
.PP
A non\-\f[CR]null\f[R] \f[CR]dtmf\f[R] doesn\(cqt mean you can send
tones yet.
Tones travel in the RTP stream alongside the audio, so the sender must
be connected and sending, and the two peers must have negotiated the
\f[CR]audio/telephone\-event\f[R] codec.
Check \f[CR]canInsertDTMF\f[R] for that, or handle the
\f[CR]InvalidStateError\f[R] that \f[CR]insertDTMF()\f[R] throws.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Sending tones on an audio track
This example adds a microphone track to a connection, then sends a dial
string once the connection is up.
\f[CR]addTrack()\f[R] returns the \f[CR]RTCRtpSender\f[R] for the track,
so there\(cqs no need to search for it.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] pc = \f[B]new\f[R] RTCPeerConnection(configuration);

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] dial(tones) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]await\f[R] navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: \f[B]true\f[R] });
  \f[B]const\f[R] [track] = stream.getAudioTracks();
  \f[B]const\f[R] sender = pc.addTrack(track, stream);

  \f[I]// The track is an audio track, so the sender has a DTMF sender\f[R]
  \f[B]const\f[R] dtmfSender = sender.dtmf;

  dtmfSender.addEventListener(\(dqtonechange\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    \f[B]if\f[R] (event.tone === \(dq\(dq) {
      console.log(\(dqFinished sending tones.\(dq);
    } \f[B]else\f[R] {
      console.log(\(gaSent tone: ${event.tone}\(ga);
    }
  });

  pc.addEventListener(\(dqconnectionstatechange\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    \f[B]if\f[R] (pc.connectionState === \(dqconnected\(dq && dtmfSender.canInsertDTMF) {
      dtmfSender.insertDTMF(tones);
    }
  });
}
.EE
.SS Finding the audio senders on a connection
Because only audio senders have a \f[CR]dtmf\f[R] object, you can use
the property to pick them out of
\f[CR]RTCPeerConnection.getSenders()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] audioSenders = pc.getSenders().filter((sender) \f[B]=>\f[R] sender.dtmf);
.EE
